On Wednesday 08 September 2004 14:08 Yoshi the Ninja
(yoshi@sbcglobal.net) wrote:

> I am trapped in a shop with a debt I cannot pay. Starving, I ran into
> the nearest shop and desperately devoured a nearby ration.  I was
> afraid
> of praying to my god and risking incurring his wrath.  

If you haven't done anything to piss your god off, and if you haven't
prayed too recently, praying when you're Weak or worse is usually safe.

> I am a pretty 
> new player (I have never killed a shopkeeper before), but I feel like
> this
> character is promising.  He is a Level 8 Ranger, whose only reliable
> weapon is a bow (which he is skilled in), and a crude dagger pulled
> off a
> dead orc (which he is also skilled in).  He has a unicorn horn (which
> I am not sure will heal him), 

It will cure sickness, confusion, hallucination, stunning, nausea,
blindness and stat loss from abuse or poison, but it won't restore lost
HP.

> several unidentified scrolls and potions 
> (which I am very afraid to use), and most importantly, a -2 armor 
> class.  What I
> need to know is: should I attack the shopkeep?  

I wouldn't unless I was *very* sure I could pull it off or die otherwise
anyway. But then I never kill peaceful creatures unless it's absolutely
necessary.

> Wonotobo is his name.  

Yes, that's a general storekeeper. Probably Ms. Wonotobo, come to think
of it.

> I have two dogs at my command (Cooper & Sirius), but I'm afraid they
> will  hinder me and get in the way of my bowshot.

> Should I read my UnID'd scrolls and hope one of them is a teleport?  

Qualified yes. Drop them first for Wonotobo to bid (don't sell yet,
unless that will cover your bill); if (s)he offers you 10 for one it's
identify, and if (s)he offers you 50 it *may* be teleport. If you get
25 or 30 or significantly more than 50 it can't *ever* be teleport; I'm
not sure about 40. If you do have an identify scroll, use it on as many
scrolls, wands or rings as it will identify that might be teleport.
Don't forget to pick up everything in the shop that you want identified
before you read the scroll; it might just give you a full-inventory
identify.

If you're really desperate, a cursed spellbook may teleport you. 

Teleporting out of the shop won't hurt your alignment if you're chaotic,
and Kops are easier to deal with than shopkeepers (but make sure you're
off the level before Wonotobo catches up with you). If you have a
*cursed* scroll of teleport, you'll even evade the Kops.

   Raisse, killed by a Kop Sergeant

